<h1>feedOmeter &amp; FeedO+: Immediate Dual-Track Strategy &amp; Project Plan</h1>
<p><strong>Production Launch Lockdown &amp; Isolated Dev/R&amp;D Pipeline</strong></p>

<hr/>

<h2>1. Executive Summary &amp; Strategy Overview</h2>

<p>To ensure maximum product velocity and zero disruption to end-users, feedOmeter is adopting a formal <strong>Dual-Track Environment Architecture</strong>:</p>

<ol>
  <li><strong>Track 1: Production Environment (feedOmeter Core)</strong> <span class="badge-prod">PROD</span>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Scope:</strong> 100% focus on rock-solid, ultra-fast, clean RSS reading.</li>
      <li><strong>Action:</strong> Revert experimental additions to keep the public build lean, pure, and bug-free.</li>
      <li><strong>Outcome:</strong> Instant launch readiness, SEO optimization, and immediate marketing execution.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Track 2: Dev &amp; R&amp;D Sandbox (FeedO+ Intelligence Hub)</strong> <span class="badge-dev">DEV / R&amp;D</span>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Scope:</strong> Aggressive feature engineering (Canonical Story model, Reddit OAuth API, Hacker News signals, Community Pulse Score, Deduplication).</li>
      <li><strong>Action:</strong> Hosted on an independent GitHub repository and secondary Cloudflare environment.</li>
      <li><strong>Outcome:</strong> Fearless experimentation with zero risk of breaking live users or burning production API limits.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ol>

<pre>
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                           PRODUCTION ENVIRONMENT                            │
│  GitHub: feedometer (main)  ──►  Cloudflare: Production Domain / Worker     │
│                                                                             │
│  • Pure, ultra-fast RSS Reader (100% stable, zero bloat)                    │
│  • Curated "Popular Feeds" Navigator &amp; Custom Themes                        │
│  • Full in-app article reading &amp; multi-device responsiveness                │
│  • Live for public users, social sharing &amp; marketing launch                 │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                     ▲
                                     │ (Tested, approved modules migrated)
                                     │
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                       DEV / R&amp;D ENVIRONMENT (FeedO+)                        │
│  GitHub: feedometer-dev     ──►  Cloudflare: Dev Worker / Staging           │
│                                                                             │
│  • Canonical Story &amp; Signal Engine (Exact URL Deduplication)                │
│  • Official Reddit OAuth 2.0 API (Real upvotes &amp; comment counts)            │
│  • Hacker News &amp; Product Hunt real-time signal stream                       │
│  • Dual-Action Cards ([Read Article] vs [Community Discussions])            │
│  • Curated Topic Bundles &amp; Community Pulse Score (0–100)                    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
</pre>

<h2>2. Key Advantages of Environmental Separation</h2>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Dimension</th>
      <th>Production Environment</th>
      <th>Dev / R&amp;D Environment (FeedO+)</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Primary Goal</strong></td>
      <td>Flawless UX, sub-second speed, 99.99% uptime</td>
      <td>Innovation, signal aggregation, rapid feature testing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Risk Tolerance</strong></td>
      <td><strong>Zero</strong> (Zero breaking changes for live users)</td>
      <td><strong>High</strong> (Experimental APIs, architectural refactors)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>API / Worker Quota</strong></td>
      <td>Dedicated 100,000 requests/day (Cloudflare Free)</td>
      <td>Independent 100,000 requests/day (Cloudflare Free)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Third-Party APIs</strong></td>
      <td>Standard RSS syndication endpoints</td>
      <td>Official Reddit OAuth 2.0, Firebase/Supabase, HN API</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Deployment Cadence</strong></td>
      <td>Scheduled, verified production releases</td>
      <td>Continuous development commits</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>3. Comprehensive Project Plan &amp; Work Breakdown Structure (WBS)</h2>

<h3>Track 1: Production Lockdown &amp; Public Launch Readiness</h3>
<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 1.1: Revert Experimental Plugin from Production</strong><br/>
Remove <code>&lt;script src="feedoplus/feedoplus.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code> from <code>index.html</code>. Ensure top-left corner exclusively displays the clean <code>READ F.M</code> logo while top-right Navigator and background switcher function seamlessly.</div>

<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 1.2: End-to-End Core Reader Regression Testing</strong><br/>
Validate default feeds (The Verge, NYT World, ScienceDaily, Wired, TechCrunch), custom user inputs, full reader modal extraction, and multi-device responsive layout.</div>

<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 1.3: Asset, Icon &amp; Metadata Audit</strong><br/>
Verify <code>favicon.ico</code>, <code>favicon.png</code> (512x512), <code>favicon.svg</code>, and OpenGraph/Twitter social sharing meta tags.</div>

<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 1.4: Production Git &amp; Cloudflare Sync</strong><br/>
Commit clean production code to the primary <code>feedometer</code> repository and verify Cloudflare Worker routes and CORS headers.</div>

<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 1.5: Public Launch Execution</strong><br/>
Kick off initial marketing, outreach, community directories, and social sharing.</div>

<h3>Track 2: Development &amp; Staging Environment Setup</h3>
<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 2.1: Initialize Secondary GitHub Repository</strong><br/>
Create repository: <code>feedometer-dev</code> (or <code>feedometer-plus</code>) and push the complete codebase including the <code>feedoplus/</code> plugin directory.</div>

<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 2.2: Setup Secondary Cloudflare Account / Worker</strong><br/>
Create new Cloudflare account/project for the dev environment and deploy <code>feedometer-dev-worker</code> with independent routing.</div>

<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 2.3: Configure Dev Environment Endpoints</strong><br/>
Point dev frontend to query <code>feedometer-dev-worker</code> and add a subtle <code>[DEV MODE]</code> indicator.</div>

<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 2.4: Validate Complete Environmental Isolation</strong><br/>
Confirm zero shared state or cross-talk between Prod and Dev environments.</div>

<h3>Track 3: Official Reddit API &amp; Data Ingestion (Dev Sandbox)</h3>
<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 3.1: Reddit Developer App Registration</strong><br/>
Register new app on Reddit Developer Portal to obtain <code>Client ID</code> and <code>Client Secret</code>.</div>

<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 3.2: OAuth 2.0 Token Manager in Cloudflare Worker</strong><br/>
Implement automated Client Credentials token exchange (<code>/api/v1/access_token</code>) with in-memory/KV token caching.</div>

<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 3.3: Structured Subreddit JSON Handler</strong><br/>
Query <code>/r/{subreddit}/hot.json</code> with Bearer token and parse clean karma scores, comment counts, author, and thumbnails.</div>

<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 3.4: Rate-Limit Monitor &amp; Fallback Mechanism</strong><br/>
Track rate-limit headers and implement graceful fallback to anonymous feeds if needed.</div>

<h3>Track 4: Canonical Story Engine &amp; URL Deduplication (Dev Sandbox)</h3>
<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 4.1: URL Normalizer &amp; Parameter Stripper</strong><br/>
Strip tracking parameters (<code>utm_*</code>, <code>ref</code>, <code>fbclid</code>, <code>gclid</code>) to resolve target canonical URLs across articles and community posts.</div>

<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 4.2: Dual-Object Data Model Implementation</strong><br/>
Implement <code>StoryItem</code> schema (external articles with attached signals) and <code>NativeDiscussionItem</code> schema (self-contained community threads).</div>

<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 4.3: Hacker News &amp; Multi-Platform Signal Ingestion</strong><br/>
Ingest Hacker News Firebase API and match stories across Reddit and primary RSS articles.</div>

<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 4.4: Dual-Action Card Interface</strong><br/>
Design card UI with primary <code>[ 📖 Read Article ]</code> and secondary <code>[ 🗨️ View Discussions ]</code> buttons with live community score counters.</div>

<h3>Track 5: Attention Intelligence &amp; Topic Bundles (Dev Sandbox)</h3>
<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 5.1: Multi-Source Topic Pack Bundles</strong><br/>
Build curated bundles (AI Builder Pack, SaaS Founder Pack, Tech Leadership).</div>

<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 5.2: Community Pulse Score Algorithm (0–100)</strong><br/>
Implement normalized scoring formula combining upvote volume, comment velocity, and multi-community spread.</div>

<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 5.3: "Why Am I Seeing This?" Explainability Popovers</strong><br/>
Build interactive popovers explaining ranking signals (e.g., <em>#1 on Hacker News, +65% velocity in 3h</em>).</div>

<h3>Track 6: Staging Validation &amp; Production Migration Protocol</h3>
<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 6.1: Quality Assurance &amp; Cross-Browser Testing</strong><br/>
Execute comprehensive QA across Chrome, Firefox, Safari, iOS, and Android.</div>

<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 6.2: Modular Release Packaging</strong><br/>
Package validated features into clean, modular pull requests / cherry-picks.</div>

<div class="task-item"><strong>Task 6.3: Seamless Production Rollout</strong><br/>
Deploy approved features to Production with zero downtime and publish release notes.</div>

<h2>4. Execution Milestones</h2>

<pre>
[ MILESTONE 1: PROD LAUNCH ] ────────► Clean, pure RSS reader live for marketing
             │
[ MILESTONE 2: DEV SANDBOX ] ────────► New GitHub + Cloudflare Dev environment active
             │
[ MILESTONE 3: REDDIT OAUTH ] ───────► Real karma &amp; comment counts streaming in Dev
             │
[ MILESTONE 4: CANONICAL ENGINE ] ───► Deduplicated master stories with multi-signals
             │
[ MILESTONE 5: MIGRATION RELEASE ] ──► FeedO+ intelligence smoothly promoted to Prod
</pre>

